### Describe the bug

When executing the `ecall` instruction followed by a non-four-byte aligned instruction (such as `nop`, `li a0, 0`, etc.), where the instruction is the one to which the `ecall` jumps, XiangShan correctly recognizes the `ecall`, but the subsequent instruction is incorrectly interpreted as `c.unimp`, triggering mismatched behavior.

Here is the disassembly of the instruction:

<img width="369" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d882ac4-c58f-4e44-889c-5701f90ebad4" />

